{
  "id": "duplicate-deleted-before-push",
  "title": "A duplicate is created and deleted offline, then pushed",
  "covers": [
    "ticket follow-up 8: a duplicate's filled fields reach the survivor even if the duplicate was deleted before push",
    "ticket follow-up 2: loser deleted_at - merge sets it only if NULL; a delete op writes it by clock"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "B, offline, adds 食べる (note L, sentence filled, T+20), changes its mind and deletes L (T+22). Then B syncs.",
    "Ops are pushed in hlc order, so the server sees note.created L first. L collides with W: merged, and L's sentence is forwarded to W.",
    "note.deleted L arrives next. A delete addressed to a loser affects only the loser, so W stays live - and keeps the sentence. Accepted trade-off.",
    "L.deleted_at: the merge set it to the merge's wall time (T+100) because it was NULL; the delete op then wins the 'deleted' register (no clock stored yet) and sets it to T+22.",
    "On phone B the delete was applied first and the merge found deleted_at already set and left it: T+22 as well."
  ],
